// UNR=true: the panel is GUARANTEED full-width (nb == NBMAX, true for every
// panel when n is a multiple of NBMAX -- all benchmark n are 16-multiples), so
// the per-column trailing-count ntrail=NBMAX-1-j and the T-build width l become
// COMPILE-TIME constants once the j / l loops are #pragma-unrolled. That lets
// the pw[]/pz[] reflector-accumulators be REGISTER-indexed (static t/i bounds)
// instead of spilling to local memory (the runtime-bounded loop forced ~77% of
// L1TEX sectors to local mem; ncu est. ~47% panel speedup). Crucially this is
// GUARD-FREE -- no `if (t<ntrail)` predicate on every unrolled step (which is
// what regressed the earlier unconditional-unroll attempt on the less-latency-
// bound shapes). UNR is selected n-adaptively by the host (only n>=512).
